-- An @nlg on a MIXFIX definition, read at a call site in the SAME module.
-- The harness is `l4 nlg` (jl4/tests-cli/Main.hs, "an @nlg on a mixfix
-- definition"); this file is outside the golden globs on purpose, and
-- nlg-mixfix-import.l4 makes the same calls across an IMPORT.
--
-- A mixfix call resolves to the operator's CANONICAL name, the slot/keyword
-- pattern `the lower of _ and _`, while the definition's head keeps only the
-- first keyword. The herald table used to be keyed on the head alone, so none
-- of the interleaved calls below found their herald.

-- Keyword-first, two keywords, herald on its own line above the head.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the smaller of %a% and %b%
`the lower of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

-- Keyword-first, herald trailing the last input: the placement the prelude's
-- `the amount by which` is written in (#788). The herald lands on `b` and is
-- moved to the rule.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount by which` a `exceeds` b @nlg the amount by which %a% exceeds %b%
  MEANS a MINUS b

-- The herald names the slots in the OTHER order: a slot is filled by the input
-- it names, not by where it sits in the sentence.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg %b% less %a%
`the shortfall of` a `against` b MEANS b MINUS a

-- Param-first infix.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg %a% and %b% together
a `plus` b MEANS a PLUS b

-- A herald that never mentions %b%: the argument is appended, not dropped.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the first of %a%
`the first of` a `then` b MEANS a

-- No herald: the call keeps the linearizer's reading.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the bare` a `and` b MEANS a PLUS b

-- Control: a PREFIX function with a herald, which has always worked.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the greater of %a% and %b%
`the greater` a b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

-- Control: a PREFIX function whose herald trails its last input, which a WITH
-- call from another module used to print a second time as that input's label.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the gap` a b @nlg the gap between %a% and %b%
  MEANS a MINUS b

-- The interleaved spelling, one call per row above.
#EVAL `the lower of` 840 `and` 160
#EVAL `the amount by which` 840 `exceeds` 160
#EVAL `the shortfall of` 160 `against` 840
#EVAL 840 `plus` 160
#EVAL `the first of` 840 `then` 160
#EVAL `the bare` 840 `and` 160
#EVAL `the greater` 3 4

-- Nested: the inner call is expanded first.
#EVAL `the lower of` (`the lower of` 5 `and` 6) `and` 7

-- The OF spelling resolves to the head keyword alone, and a WITH call to the
-- head name. Neither goes through the canonical name, and neither may change.
#EVAL `the lower of` OF 840, 160
#EVAL `the amount by which` OF 840, 160
#EVAL `the lower of` WITH a IS 840, b IS 160
#EVAL `the amount by which` WITH a IS 840, b IS 160

-- The prefix control, positional and WITH.
#EVAL `the gap` 840 160
#EVAL `the gap` WITH a IS 840, b IS 160

-- Render rows. `l4 nlg` prints directives only, so these add nothing to the
-- output above; they give `l4 render` a call to each function inside the body
-- of another rule, which is the other place a herald is read at a call site.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`render lower` n MEANS `the lower of` n `and` 100

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`render exceeds` n MEANS `the amount by which` n `exceeds` 100

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`render shortfall` n MEANS `the shortfall of` n `against` 100

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`render plus` n MEANS n `plus` 100

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`render first` n MEANS `the first of` n `then` 100

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`render bare` n MEANS `the bare` n `and` 100

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`render greater` n MEANS `the greater` n 100

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`render nested` n MEANS `the lower of` (`the lower of` n `and` 100) `and` 200

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`render of` n MEANS `the lower of` OF n, 100
